"decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["attest.py:555 `if kind == \"completion-verifier\":` — the validity path is ALREADY parameterized for this attestation kind (material recompute + reopen check)","attest.py:544-553 reopen invalidation (`last_reopened_at`, verdict `stale-reopened`) — matches the plan's 'Reject attestations invalidated by a later reopen'","reuse.py:53 idempotent_reuse docstring: 'reuse an existing, still-valid plan-review attestation INSTEAD of re-running the billable multi-pass LLM review ... binds the current material fingerprint, whose reviewed code has not drifted ... and which post-dates any reopen' — the same reuse contract this plan re-specifies","verify_opcert.py:214-267 already composes opcert.opcert_from_record + _authoritative_material + trusted_env.verify_required_environment (SHA + material + pinned-key binding)","The plan text names none of these; it presents each check as a new requirement to implement"],"finding":"The Repair plan re-enumerates a bespoke per-check attested-completion validator (cryptographic op-cert certify, PASS-manifest, verified-at-sha equality, material-fingerprint equality, reopen invalidation, ineligible-fallthrough) without referencing the existing, already-completion-verifier-aware validity machinery it duplicates: compute_validity(kind='completion-verifier') (attest.py:555, incl. the reopen check at 544-553 and material recompute at 562-583), the claim_gate_check wrapper (attest_gate.py:99), the analogous idempotent_reuse short-circuit (reuse.py:53), and verify_opcert.py's op-cert-read + verify_required_environment assembly.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2d35813f8d6ef17b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Repair plan (all bullets) + Proven root cause","norm_id":"n7a74f73ab7a082eb","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer writes a fresh signature/SHA/material/reopen validator that drifts from compute_validity's completion-verifier semantics (e.g. legacy-material tolerance via _legacy_material_ok, unverifiable-material fail-closed) and diverges under future edits"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Route the reuse decision through the existing completion-verifier validity path (compute_validity / claim_gate_check style) and only ADD the two things it does not yet cover for an in-progress close: (a) accepting a not-yet-closed ticket at close time, and (b) the verified-at-sha == resolved-close-target-SHA equality; return the reused PASS in the same shape idempotent_reuse already uses.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the pre-close reuse eligibility decision must NOT be gated on ticket status='closed' (the reopen/material/SHA/crypto checks apply, but the compute_validity 'not-closed' guard must be omitted or bypassed, since the reuse check runs while the ticket is still in progress).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/unit/test_compute_validity.py:23-28 — compute_validity(..., status='open', 'completion-verifier') returns valid False / verdict 'not-closed'","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:405 compute_validity — completion arm keys on ticket_state status/last_reopened_at/material","Plan Context: 'created a certified same-ref completion record on an in-progress bug, then closed at that exact SHA' — the reuse check must fire while status is in-progress"],"finding":"The reuse eligibility checks the plan enumerates (crypto-certify, PASS, SHA-pin equality, material-fingerprint equality, reopen invalidation) map almost exactly onto compute_validity's completion arm, but that arm also returns verdict='not-closed' for any status != 'closed'. The reuse decision runs on an IN-PROGRESS ticket (the stated trigger precondition), so delegating eligibility to compute_validity would wrongly reject every reusable attestation, silently defeating the whole feature and falling through to the provider.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8a63417dd52f2fee","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Repair plan (\"Reject attestations invalidated by a later reopen\"); Test contract card trigger_preconditions (\"ticket is in progress\")","norm_id":"ncf192c98029a237d","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer reuses compute_validity(kind='completion-verifier') for the eligibility gate; every reuse is rejected as 'not-closed' and the provider is still called once, so AC1 (zero provider calls) can never pass."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a repair-plan sentence: assemble the reuse eligibility from the component checks (verify_signature crypto, manifest PASS, verified_at_sha equality, current_material_fingerprint equality, last_reopened_at < signed_at) directly, WITHOUT the compute_validity 'not-closed' status guard, because the decision runs on the still-in-progress ticket being closed.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"bina